 "id": "ultra-apple",
 "name": "Golden apple",
 "optionNote": "A golden apple gives Minecraft's absorption hearts: extra hearts in gold that sit on top of your health. Here all ten hearts are gold (#FFD43B) and the 5-hour % becomes a bold gold ∞. The sun ☼ stays in the gutter so the line still starts with the day, but there is no clock: nothing resets. Gold is used nowhere else on the hearts row, so it can only mean \"no 5-hour limit\".",
 "title": "No 5-hour limit (the Ultra plan)",
 "intro": "On the Ultra plan Claude Code sends no five_hour limit at all, only the week. Hungerbar 1.0 then draws a grey ? and ten dark hearts, which reads as \"no health left\" or \"something broke\", when it really means \"no 5-hour limit to run out of\". These options say \"unlimited\" instead. Hardcore hearts were ruled out: in Minecraft they mean one life only (permadeath), the opposite of an unlimited plan.",
